# The Overview tiles of the realm places (/places?realm=<id>): an app or a
# staging site, its link, and the commands that run it (sd:6162, sd:6164).
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/place-tiles.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the lines
# below are examples. Folders, hosts and commands are this machine's, so
# they live here, never in the checkout or in a setting the page writes.
#
#   tile|<realm>|<tile>|<label>|<folder>|<url or ->
#   act|<tile>|<label>|<command>
#
# <realm> is an id in dashboard.realms; <tile> is a lower-case id of your
# own. Visit opens <url>; each Overview read asks it once and says whether
# it answers. Each act line is a button. Its command is split as a shell
# would split it, with no shell: no pipe, no $VAR, no ~. It runs in
# <folder>, in its own session, with its output in
# ~/.local/state/system/place-tiles/<realm>/<tile>/<action>/start.log.
# Wrap a command that needs a shell or a login PATH: /bin/zsh -lc "...".
# A folder that is not on this machine shows the tile, its link and the
# reason, and runs nothing.

tile|work|simulator|World simulator|~/repos/example-org/example-simulator|http://127.0.0.1:8740/studio
act|simulator|Start|./example-simulator.sh studio
act|simulator|Stop|./example-simulator.sh studio-stop
act|simulator|Update|git pull --ff-only

tile|acme|staging|Staging site|~/deploy/acme-website|https://staging.example.test
act|staging|Deploy|/bin/zsh -lc "npm run staging:deploy"
act|staging|Tear down|/bin/zsh -lc "npm run staging:down"
act|staging|Refresh|/bin/zsh -lc "npm run staging:up"
